From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:40:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] toolchain: gcc: write each LTRANS job's output whole

When lto-wrapper runs a link's LTRANS jobs in parallel through make, the
jobs write their diagnostics to the same stream as they go, in pieces,
and those of jobs running at once interleave: a warning then follows
another job's chain of inlined calls, and a reader of the build log
places it in the wrong function or in none. A package built without the
jobserver has lto-wrapper start such a make with its own number of jobs
(-flto=auto), whose output no make above it holds back.

Add a patch to GCC that runs that make with --output-sync=target, which
writes each job's output once the job ends. The patch is meant for GCC
upstream.

Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 ...write-each-LTRANS-job-s-output-whole.patch | 34 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 toolchain/gcc/patches-15.x/990-lto-wrapper-write-each-LTRANS-job-s-output-whole.patch

diff --git a/toolchain/gcc/patches-15.x/990-lto-wrapper-write-each-LTRANS-job-s-output-whole.patch b/toolchain/gcc/patches-15.x/990-lto-wrapper-write-each-LTRANS-job-s-output-whole.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..dcc9727
--- /dev/null
+++ b/toolchain/gcc/patches-15.x/990-lto-wrapper-write-each-LTRANS-job-s-output-whole.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,34 @@
+From: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+Subject: [PATCH] lto-wrapper: write each LTRANS job's output whole
+
+When lto-wrapper runs the LTRANS jobs in parallel through make, every
+job writes its diagnostics to the same stream as it goes. A diagnostic
+is written in pieces, its "In function" context and its chain of
+inlined calls apart from the message itself, so the pieces of jobs
+running at once interleave: a warning then follows another job's
+context, and a reader of the build log places it in the wrong function
+or in none.
+
+Run make with --output-sync=target, which writes each job's output once
+the job ends. Under a jobserver the jobs still run in parallel; only
+their output is held back. lto-wrapper already runs make for parallel
+LTRANS, and GNU make has had the option since 4.0.
+
+gcc/ChangeLog:
+
+	* lto-wrapper.cc (run_gcc): Run make with --output-sync=target.
+
+Signed-off-by: kiritantakechi <kiritantakechi@gmail.com>
+---
+--- a/gcc/lto-wrapper.cc
++++ b/gcc/lto-wrapper.cc
+@@ -2194,6 +2194,9 @@
+ 			auto_parallel ? nthreads_var : parallel);
+ 	      obstack_ptr_grow (&argv_obstack, jobs);
+ 	    }
++	  /* Write each LTRANS job's output whole once the job ends, so that
++	     the diagnostics of jobs running at once do not interleave.  */
++	  obstack_ptr_grow (&argv_obstack, "--output-sync=target");
+ 	  obstack_ptr_grow (&argv_obstack, "all");
+ 	  obstack_ptr_grow (&argv_obstack, NULL);
+ 	  new_argv = XOBFINISH (&argv_obstack, const char **);
